    // Battle 33 is a close fight under the matrix's spawn jitter (Q0041, Q0044). With the
    // zealot's StarCraft II weapon (damage point 0, every 21 ticks, range 0.1, backswing 9;
    // plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP4), the marine's (damage point 1, backswing 13;
    // WP6; speed 0.126 per tick, WP7), StarCraft II firing arcs (WP17 commit d: both fire within
    // 11.25 degrees of their facing), hull turning (WP17 commit f: both turn 55.99 degrees per
    // tick, where they turned instantly), a swing that starts on the tick its turn aligns it
    // (plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP1, M-22), StarCraft II's keep-target rule (WP4,
    // B-9: a unit whose target is out of weapon reach takes the closest candidate, so a chasing
    // zealot no longer follows its first marine while another is up to 1.0 closer), StarCraft
    // II's scan ranges measured edge to edge (WP14 Amendment 7, Q0057: the marine 5.5, the
    // zealot 5, beyond both radii; they were 9 and 9) and the zealot's second blade 5 ticks after
    // its first (plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP5, B-2: StarCraft II's PsiBladesBurst; it
    // landed on the swing's tick before) and StarCraft II's acquisition arc (WP10, B-29: a new
    // target must be faced exactly, `Arc` 0, before the first swing) and StarCraft II's random
    // firing delay (WP11, B-3: each attack adds -0.0625 to 0.125 Normal s, drawn per attack), on
    // 68 seeds (the four of record plus 64 jittered ones, jitter 0.12) the marines win 41, the
    // zealots win 10 and 17 are unresolved at 500 ticks; marine survivors average 4.32 (SD 3.02,
    // range 0 to 10), zealot survivors 0.74 (SD 1.13, range 0 to 5). Before B-3 it was 55 / 6 / 7
    // (5.53); before B-29 54 / 7 / 7 (5.29); before B-2
    // 21 / 37 / 10 (2.06); with the edge rule alone (scan 9 / 9) 19 / 41 / 8 (1.69),
    // before it 20 / 35 / 13 (1.85), before B-9 37 / 20 / 11 (3.62), before WP1 39 / 20 / 9
    // (3.87), after the arcs 43 / 16 / 9 (4.38), before WP17 42 / 18 / 8 (4.03), after combat
    // alignment WP4 alone 30 / 24 / 14 (3.09), and before that WP4 a marine win on 61 of the 68
    // (7.41). The expectation is the smallest ranges that hold on all 20 matrix seeds since B-9
    // (orchestrator, plan Amendment 5; the seeds of record are 9-0, 3-0, 6-0 and 7-0, marines -
    // zealots left; B-2 set them to blue 0 to 13 and red 0 to 3; since B-29 the marines win 18 of
    // the 20 seeds, blue 1 to 13 and red 0 to 2; since B-3 they win 12, the zealots 1, blue 0 to
    // 9 and red 0 to 3, and the seeds of record are 5-0, 9-0, 2-1 and 8-0); a seed outside them is re-recorded by the commit that causes it. What
    // varies is how many zealots reach the marines at once.
    // Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment.md §16 (WP14 Amendment 7) and
    // §14.7 (§14.4 for the arcs, §6, §5 and §3 for WP7, WP6 and WP4, and §1 for the earlier
    // figures, from docs/evidence/2026-11-03-battle-33-investigation.md §4.2), and
    // docs/evidence/2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes.md §12 (B-3), §11 (B-29), §5.3 (B-2), §4.6 (B-9) and §1
    // (WP1).
    (
        name: "33_24_marines_vs_12_zealots",
